Vendored verbatim from https://github.com/ppazos/cabolabs-ehrserver
opts/e9d13294-bce7-44e7-9635-8e906da0c914/bkp_for_testing/b498242e-633a-4127-94db-0dedaa3151ba.opt
— the CaboLabs EHRServer "Test all datatypes" openEHR Operational Template (ADL 1.4
OPT). It is a synthetic template that deliberately exercises every openEHR RM datatype,
authored by CaboLabs and licensed Apache-2.0 (no clinical-archetype CC-BY-SA provenance).

Vendored here as the on-gate round-trip law fixture for the openEHR constraints axis: it
is the only real, permissively-licensed OPT that carries BOTH a C_DATE_TIME constraint
(a `<pattern>yyyy-mm-ddTHH:MM:SS</pattern>` validity pattern) and a C_DV_ORDINAL
constraint (a `<list>` of `<value>` integer + `<defining_code>` symbol pairs) — the two
constraint families no available clinical OPT carries together. It is a law fixture ONLY
(it proves recover∘lift = id on parsed XML for those families); being a synthetic
datatype-exercising template, it is NOT wired as a production generator input and its
constraints do not flow into the shipped gmeow.gts.
